<h3 class="govuk-heading-m">Why this matters</h3>

<p class="govuk-body">Not every demo audience has a phone to hand. The companion app embeds the <a href="https://aws.amazon.com/chime/chime-sdk/" class="govuk-link">Amazon Chime SDK</a>, which bridges into the same Connect contact flow that PSTN calls use. The audio is browser-mediated, but everything downstream &mdash; Lex, the Bedrock Knowledge Base, Connect Cases, Customer Profiles &mdash; is identical to a phone call.</p>

<h3 class="govuk-heading-m">What to do</h3>

<ol class="govuk-list govuk-list--number govuk-list--spaced">
  <li>Open the companion web app at the <code>CompanionUrl</code> output. Look at the top of the right-hand pane for the chat input row.</li>
  <li>Click the <strong>Call via browser</strong> button next to the chat input.</li>
  <li>Your browser pops up a microphone permission dialog. Click <strong>Allow</strong>. Without microphone access the call cannot connect.</li>
  <li>Wait about three seconds. The status text reads "starting&hellip;" then "loading SDK&hellip;" then <strong>"call connected"</strong>.</li>
  <li>Speak. Try the bin-collection script from step 1 or the fly-tip script from step 2.</li>
  <li>The bot replies through your laptop speakers. The transcript and case panes update live, just like for a PSTN call.</li>
</ol>

<h3 class="govuk-heading-m">Bonus: video and screen share</h3>

<p class="govuk-body">After the audio call connects, two more buttons appear next to "End call":</p>

<ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
  <li><strong>Add video</strong> &mdash; turns on your webcam. Your tile appears under the chat. The bot doesn't process the video stream directly today, but in a real deployment you could route the video to a human agent for sign language interpretation.</li>
  <li><strong>Share screen</strong> &mdash; shares your screen into the call. Useful when an agent is helping a resident navigate something visual (a planning portal, a benefits form).</li>
</ul>

<div class="govuk-inset-text">
  <p class="govuk-body">The call ends when you click <strong>End call</strong> or close the tab. There's no PSTN charge because no phone number was involved &mdash; the audio rides over WebRTC into Chime, then bridges into Connect. Cost-wise, this is the cheapest way to demo voice to a remote audience.</p>
</div>
